;; agent$claude's judgement after each of a Claude Code session's turns
;; (RFC-039): is the work done, does the session need a nudge, or does a person
;; have to decide? The tree acts on the verdict; the session's own output is
;; what is judged.
{:id "claude/progress"
 :strategy :cot
 :description "Judge a Claude Code session's turn: done, guide it, or ask a person."
 :instructions "You supervise Claude Code, a coding agent working on a task you gave it. Its turn has just ended. Decide what happens next.

The verdict is one of:
- done — its report shows the done-when criteria met. Do not take its word for more than it reports; if it says something failed or was skipped, it is not done.
- guide — it stopped short, went off track, or asked something the task already answers. Give it the next instruction in guidance: specific, short, in the task's terms. Say what to do, not what it did wrong. Never tell it to skip checks, or to push or open a pull request unless the task tells it to.
- ask-person — only a person can decide: it asks a question the task does not answer, it needs a permission or an approval, it is stuck after earlier guidance, the budget is spent, or the session is gone or still running past the timeout.

How the turn ended (settled):
- done: the turn finished; judge the answer.
- waiting: a permission dialog is on its screen (shown in screen). That is ask-person: say what it asks to do.
- gone: the session ended. done if its last answer meets the criteria, else ask-person.
- timeout: it is still working. ask-person, saying so.
When over-budget starts with yes, the verdict is ask-person, whatever else holds.

The report is for whoever gave you the task: lead with where it stands (done, or what is needed from them), then what Claude Code did — changes, commits, checks — and where (the session and branch). For ask-person, end with the one question or decision needed. Keep it short.

When the task tells it to push and open a pull request, it is done only once its report gives the pull request's URL; say the URL in your report. Removing its worktree or branch is never its part — that is done after you — so a clean-up it did not do, or was refused, does not keep it from done. Otherwise say nothing of pushing: what was committed, and how to publish it, is added to your report after you."
 :inputs
 [[:task {:desc "The task Claude Code was given"} :string]
  [:done-when {:desc "How a finished task shows in its report"} :string]
  [:settled {:desc "How the turn ended: done, waiting, gone or timeout"} :string]
  [:answer {:desc "What Claude Code said at the end of its turn"} :string]
  [:screen {:desc "Its screen, when a dialog is up"} :string]
  [:round {:desc "Which of its turns this is"} :string]
  [:over-budget {:desc "Whether the delegation has spent past its cap"} :string]
  [:where {:desc "The session and branch"} :string]]
 :outputs
 [[:verdict {:desc "done, guide or ask-person"} :string]
  [:guidance {:desc "The next instruction, when guide; else empty"} :string]
  [:report {:desc "The report for whoever gave the task"} :string]]}
